WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.958
A bad map shrinks a good mission. A flat location turns danger into bookkeeping.

2
00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:19.917
RUNSITE is for the kind of space that should feel legible, threatening, and worth arguing about before the first door even opens.

3
00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:29.875
A site unfolds in layers. Approach. Floor plan. Cameras. Exits. Hidden routes. Astral residue. Pressure points.

4
00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:39.833
The corners players will immediately try to exploit and the mistakes that will wake the building up around them.

5
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:49.792
Player view stays readable. GM view keeps the teeth behind the curtain.

6
00:00:49.792 --> 00:00:59.750
Hotspots prepare the moments that matter without scripting the route in advance.

7
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:09.708
The crew can scout, fight, improvise, and plan around a place instead of a paragraph.

8
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:19.667
If they go loud, the site should answer like a living problem. If they go quiet, it should still have texture.

9
00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:29.625
RUNSITE makes locations matter before the breach, during the run, and in the memory that follows.
